W: 2. Here's a health to the ox and to his long tail,
W: Pray God send our master a good cask of ale;
W: A good cask of ale as e'er I did see,
W: In the wassail bowl we'll drink unto thee.
W:
W: 3. Come butler come fill us a bowl of the best,
W: Then we pray that your soul in heaven may rest;
W: But if you do bring us a bowl of the small,
W: Then down shall go butler, bowl and all.
W:
W: 4. Then here's to the maid in lily white smock,
W: Who tripped to the door and slipped back the lock,
W: And slipped back the lock, and pulled back the pin,
W: For to let these jolly wassailers walk in.
%
